# Wallpaper plugins that are known to animate, one plugin id per line.
#
# The performance mode reads this to decide whether to stop the audio
# spectrum. It stops it only when an animated wallpaper is running on a
# screen that is not showing ours: if our own wallpaper is on every
# screen there is nothing to defer to, and going quiet would be giving
# up the only animation on the desktop for the sake of a wallpaper that
# is not there.
#
# This is your statement about your own desktop, so it is yours to edit.
# Add a line when you install something that animates; it takes effect on
# the next detector pass, within a couple of seconds. Remove a line and
# the spectrum comes back.
#
# It is a list and it can always be out of date. The project does not
# have to know about a plugin for it to be able to cooperate: a
# third-party animated wallpaper can read the published signal directly
# and yield on its own, which is the contract in docs/CONTRATTO-resa.md.
# This list is only for the ones we cannot make cooperate.

# Video wallpaper. Decodes a file continuously.
luisbocanegra.smart.video.wallpaper.reborn

# Static and near-static, listed so the reasoning is visible rather than
# implied. A single photograph costs nothing after the first paint, and
# org.kde.potd and org.kde.slideshow change at most hourly or daily.
# org.kde.image
# org.kde.color
# org.kde.potd
# org.kde.slideshow
# org.kde.tiled
# org.kde.hunyango
